<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea July oil products exports up 54 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>S.Korea July oil products exports up 54 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's oil products exports, excluding bunkering for foreign ships but including sales to U.S. military in South Korea, stood at 17.6 million barrels in July, up 54 percent from 11.4 million a year ago, the Korea Petroleum Association said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Product exports during the first seven months of this year totalled 84.58 million barrels, it said without giving a comparative figure for the same 1995 period.</p>
<p>Major Destinations (in 1,000 barrels, figures in brackets are FOB prices in million U.S. dollars, comparative figures unavailable):  </p>
<p>			    July			  Jan-July</p>
<p>   Japan	  6,693.4 (144.2)	     35,863.8 (770.3)</p>
<p>   China	  4,326.4  (86.5)	     18,539.8 (363.7)</p>
<p>   Hongkong     2,189.1  (54.6)		6,883.8 (171.5)</p>
<p>   Thailand     1,111.4  (27.1)		7,212.5 (186.0)</p>
<p>   Singapore    1,098.6  (20.3)		2,796.7  (56.5)</p>
<p>   U.S.	     601.1  (11.6)		2,739.1  (53.4)</p>
<p>   Taiwan	    97.6   (1.3)		2,131.9  (43.3)</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
